  "scope": "Opt-in regional inference memory observations. Synthetic CPU tests and fresh-process smoke runs only; CUDA API sequencing/device selection is mocked. No GPU, original-data, representative capacity or throughput measurement.",
  "implementation": [
    "--profile_memory is opt-in for both single and ensemble regional commands; the default does not initialize the profiler or add a metadata field.",
    "Memory collection begins after the first checkpoint/configuration preflight and accumulator policy check, before first model construction. All ensemble members retain their existing simultaneous residency.",
    "Phases observe model residency, completed inference/normalization/host copies and the latest metadata-ready point after exports/statistics, before JSON encoding.",
    "Process RSS and getrusage process-lifetime high-water RSS retain their distinct sources. Lifetime peaks include pre-profile work; Linux KiB/macOS bytes convert explicitly, and unsupported platforms record null high-water RSS.",
    "The selected CUDA device is synchronized; PyTorch allocator peak counters reset once and then remain cumulative. GPU identity/capacity and Torch build are recorded; other allocators, contexts/processes and free/whole-device peak memory are excluded.",
    "Failed primary metadata collection leaves no success sidecar after output replacement. Existing artifact planning and accumulator refusal still apply."
